  "text": "Recipe: Steamed Bean Dumplings\nCreator: Gurmeet Manku\nCategory: Dumplings\nIngredients: toor dal, mint, cilantro, cumin powder, ginger powder, black pepper, cardamom powder, goji berries, mulberries, cranberries, barberries, golden berries, shishito peppers, Meyer lemon, Meyer lemon peels, dried herbs & spice mixes\nCooking methods: steam, no-cook\nInstructions: DUMPLINGS: Soak toor dal overnight. Drain all water. Combine with some fresh mint, cilantro & spices like cumin powder, ginger powder, black pepper & cardamom powder. Turn into paste with high speed blender. Make interesting ball-like shapes and steam in a steamer. DRESSING: Soaked dried berries (goji berries, mulberries, cranberries, barberries, golden berries, ...), shishito peppers and Meyer lemon peels, mixed together. We may add dried herbs & spice mixes for additional flavor.\nNotes: DUMPLINGS, DRESSING. A recipe with BEANS (toor dal), RAINBOW VEGGIES (shishito peppers), LIME-LEMON-VINEGAR (Meyer lemon), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
